# {{ project_name }}

Multi-app FastAPI project generated by ZodiacCore.

It mounts two independent sub-applications sharing a single database and cache
backend managed by the parent process.

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Service |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | parent |
| `POST` | `/users/api/v1/users` | users |
| `GET` | `/users/api/v1/users` | users |
| `GET` | `/users/api/v1/info` | users |
| `POST` | `/orders/api/v1/orders` | orders |
| `GET` | `/orders/api/v1/orders` | orders |
| `GET` | `/orders/api/v1/info` | orders |

List endpoints support Zodiac pagination and sorting query parameters, plus a
template-level `keyword` filter:

```bash
GET /users/api/v1/users?page=1&size=20&sort=name:desc&keyword=ada
GET /orders/api/v1/orders?page=1&size=20&sort=name:desc&keyword=book
```

## Architecture

Each sub-application follows the standard ZodiacCore 3-tier architecture with
dependency injection:

```
orders/                      users/
├── api/                     ├── api/
│   ├── router.py            │   ├── router.py
│   ├── routers/             │   ├── routers/
│   └── schemas/             │   └── schemas/
├── application/services/    ├── application/services/
├── core/container.py        ├── core/container.py
└── infrastructure/database/ └── infrastructure/database/
```

Middleware (trace ID, service name, access log) is registered on each
sub-application to avoid double-wrapping of requests.

## Agent Workflow

This project includes `AGENTS.md` so teams can use Codex with the project
conventions for FastAPI, pytest, and ZodiacCore.

## Add A Sub-Application

Generate a new service skeleton from the project root:

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run zodiac add sub-app billing
```

The command does not edit `main.py`. Follow the printed import, lifespan, and
mount instructions, or ask Codex to complete and test the integration.

To use the CLI without installing development dependencies, run it as a
one-shot tool instead:

```bash
uvx --from "zodiac-core[zodiac]" zodiac add sub-app billing
```

## Run

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run uvicorn main:app --reload --no-access-log
```

## Test

```bash
uv run pytest
```
